stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> OPEN: employee raises dispute (POST /disputes)

    OPEN --> UNDER_REVIEW: payroll officer picks it up / is assigned

    UNDER_REVIEW --> PAYROLL_CORRECTION_REQUIRED: investigation shows the\ncalculation itself was wrong
    UNDER_REVIEW --> REJECTED: dispute found invalid
    UNDER_REVIEW --> RESOLVED: dispute valid but needs\nonly an explanation, no recalculation

    PAYROLL_CORRECTION_REQUIRED --> CORRECTION_IN_PROGRESS: correction PayrollRun created\n(RunType=Correction, ParentRunId=original)

    CORRECTION_IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED: correction run approved,\nnew SalarySlip generated (Version+1),\nold slip superseded (not deleted)

    RESOLVED --> [*]
    REJECTED --> [*]

    note right of PAYROLL_CORRECTION_REQUIRED
        Correction run contains ONLY the
        disputed employee's entry and goes
        through the SAME approval workflow
        as a regular run (§18.4)
    end note

    note right of RESOLVED
        Both resolution paths (with or
        without correction) converge here —
        difference amount, if any, is tracked
        separately for accounting reconciliation
    end note
